ddlistener} — Add a new listener to the server.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::addProcess} — Add a user defined swoole_process to the server.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::after} — Trigger a callback function after a period of time.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::bind} — Bind the connection to a user defined user ID.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::clearTimer} — Stop and destroy a timer.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::close} — Close a connection to the client.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::confirm} — Check status of the connection.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::connection_info} — Get the connection info by file description.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::connection_list} — Get all of the established connections.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::__construct} — Construct a Swoole server.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::defer} — Delay execution of the callback function at the end of current EventLoop.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::exist} — Check if the connection is existed.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::finish} — Used in task process for sending result to the worker process when the task is finished.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::getClientInfo} — Get the connection info by file description.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::getClientList} — Get all of the established connections.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::getLastError} — Get the error code of the most recent error.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::heartbeat} — Check all the connections on the server.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::listen} — Listen on the given IP and port, socket type.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::on} — Register a callback function by event name.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::pause} — Stop receiving data from the connection.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::protect} — Set the connection to be protected mode.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::reload} — Restart all the worker process.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::resume} — Start receiving data from the connection.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::send} — Send data to the client.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::sendfile} — Send file to the connection.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::sendMessage} — Send message to worker processes by ID.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::sendto} — Send data to the remote UDP address.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::sendwait} — Send data to the remote socket in the blocking way.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::set} — Set the runtime settings of the swoole server.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::shutdown} — Shutdown the master server process, this function can be called in worker processes.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::start} — Start the Swoole server.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::stats} — Get the stats of the Swoole server.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::stop} — Stop the Swoole server.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::task} — Send data to the task worker processes.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::taskwait} — Send data to the task worker processes in blocking way.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::taskWaitMulti} — Execute multiple tasks concurrently.</li><li>{@link Swoole\Server::tick} — Repeats a given function at every given time-interval.</li></ul></div>
